    {
      "label": "District Electoral Areas Commissioner (Northern Ireland) (Amendment) Order 2007 (S.I. 2007 No. 612 (N.I. 4))",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisi/2007/612",
      "note": "Made 6 Mar 2007, in force 14 days later. Substituted Articles 2 and 3 of the District Electoral Areas Commissioner (Northern Ireland) Order 1984: a District Electoral Areas Commissioner is appointed once a Local Government Boundaries Commissioner is appointed, and reports on the grouping of wards into electoral areas after the boundaries order under section 50(10) of the Local Government Act (Northern Ireland) 1972 is made, the sequence the 2012-13 review followed."
    },
    {
      "label": "District Electoral Areas Commissioner (Northern Ireland) (Amendment) Order 2009 (S.I. 2009 No. 3016)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2009/3016",
      "note": "Made 17 Nov 2009, in force the next day. Amended the Commissioner's procedure in Schedule 2 to the 1984 Order (eight weeks, not one month, for representations on provisional recommendations) and, where a boundaries order changes the number of districts, read references to a district's council as the council of the former district it incorporates, as applied in the review of the 11 districts' electoral areas."
    },
    {
      "label": "District Electoral Areas Commissioner (Northern Ireland) Order 2012 (S.I. 2012 No. 3074)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2012/3074",
      "note": "Made 12 Dec 2012, in force the next day, two weeks after the Local Government (Boundaries) Order (Northern Ireland) 2012. Amended the 1984 Order so that the Secretary of State must appoint a District Electoral Areas Commissioner as soon as practicable after a boundaries order under section 50(10) of the Local Government Act (Northern Ireland) 1972 is made: the appointment that produced this edition's electoral areas."
    },
    {
      "label": "District Electoral Areas (Northern Ireland) Order 2014 (S.I. 2014 No. 270)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2014/270",
      "note": "Made 11 Feb 2014; in force the next day for proceedings for the local elections of 22 May 2014 and for all other purposes on 22 May 2014. Divides each of the 11 districts of the Local Government (Boundaries) Order (Northern Ireland) 2012 into the district electoral areas named in the Schedule, each comprising the wards and returning the number of councillors listed there, and revokes the District Electoral Areas (Northern Ireland) Order 1993."
    }
